  "generated_text": "1. Recognize that \\(w^4 - 16\\) is a difference of squares.\n2. A difference of squares can be factored using the formula \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\).\n3. Here, \\(w^4 - 16\\) can be written as \\((w^2)^2 - 4^2\\).\n4. Apply the difference of squares formula:\n   \\[\n   w^4 - 16 = (w^2 - 4)(w^2 + 4)\n   \\]\n5. Notice that \\(w^2 - 4\\) and \\(w^2 + 4\\) are both differences of squares.\n6. Factor \\(w^2 - 4\\) as \\((w - 2)(w + 2)\\).\n7. Factor \\(w^2 + 4\\) as \\((w - 2)(w + 2)\\).\n\nCombining all factors, the complete factorization of \\(w^4 - 16\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(w - 2)(w + 2)(w - 2)(w + 2)}\n\\]",
